          <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-normal text-ink sm:text-4xl">
            When the Supplement applies, and when it can be reduced.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
            The FERS Special Retirement Supplement is not Social Security and is not paid automatically to every federal retiree.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Typical eligibility</h3>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
              <li>Immediate retirement before age 62</li>
              <li>30 years of service, 20 years at age 60, or special category eligibility</li>
              <li>Entitled to a Social Security benefit</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Important limitation</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
              The Supplement is subject to an earnings test before age 62. Earning too much can reduce or eliminate the payment for that year. This calculator uses an approximate method and does not calculate the earnings test.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

